    "body": "### Finding Description and Impact\n\n#### Background: Fee-on-Transfer Tokens\n\nFee-on-transfer (FoT) tokens automatically deduct a percentage during every transfer. When you call `transfer(recipient, 100)`, the recipient receives less than 100 tokens because a fee is taken. Common examples:\n\n| Token | Fee |\n|-------|-----|\n| PAXG (Paxos Gold) | 0.02% |\n| STA (Statera) | 1% |\n| USDT (configurable) | Up to 0.1% |\n| Various deflationary tokens | 1-10% |\n\n#### Root Cause Analysis\n\nThe `increaseTokenBalance()` function assumes that the amount requested equals the amount received:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender)) \n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + amount); // @audit - Credits full 'amount'\n}\n```\n\nThe problem:\n1. User calls `increaseTokenBalance(user, FOT_TOKEN, 1000)`\n2. `safeTransferFrom` transfers 1000 tokens, but FoT takes 1% fee\n3. Contract actually receives 990 tokens\n4. `creatorBalance[user][FOT_TOKEN]` is credited with 1000 (not 990!)\n\nThis creates an ever-growing deficit between recorded balances and actual token holdings.\n\n#### The Insolvency Math\n\nLet's trace through with a 1% fee token:\n\n**Deposit Phase:**\n```\nAlice deposits 1000 → Contract receives 990 → creatorBalance[Alice] = 1000\nBob deposits 1000   → Contract receives 990 → creatorBalance[Bob] = 1000\nCharlie deposits 1000 → Contract receives 990 → creatorBalance[Charlie] = 1000\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nTotal recorded: 3000 tokens\nActual balance: 2970 tokens\nDEFICIT: 30 tokens\n```\n\n**Withdrawal Phase:**\n```\nAlice withdraws 1000  → SUCCESS (2970 - 1000 = 1970 remaining)\nBob withdraws 1000    → SUCCESS (1970 - 1000 = 970 remaining)\nCharlie withdraws 1000 → FAILS! (only 970 available, needs 1000)\n```\n\nCharlie is the victim. He deposited legitimately but cannot withdraw because earlier users took more than their fair share of the actual tokens.\n\n#### Impact Assessment\n\n**Severity: HIGH** - Guaranteed fund loss for some users\n\n**1. Guaranteed Insolvency:**\nWith $n$ users each depositing amount $A$ with fee rate $f$:\n- Total recorded: $n \\times A$\n- Actual received: $n \\times A \\times (1-f)$\n- Deficit: $n \\times A \\times f$\n\nFor 100 users depositing 1000 tokens each with 1% fee:\n- Recorded: 100,000 tokens\n- Actual: 99,000 tokens\n- Deficit: 1,000 tokens\n\n**2. Last-User-Loses:**\nThe deficit isn't distributed fairly. Whoever withdraws last bears the entire accumulated loss. This creates a \"bank run\" incentive where users race to withdraw before others.\n\n**3. Silent Accounting Corruption:**\nNo errors occur during deposits. The `creatorBalance` mapping looks correct. Users have no indication of the problem until mass withdrawals begin.\n\n**4. Compounding Effect:**\nEach deposit increases the deficit. More users = larger gap = more severe loss for late withdrawers.\n\n**5. Campaign Creation Impact:**\nThe same issue exists in `_pullTokens()` for campaign creation. Campaigns may be underfunded, meaning the distributor receives fewer tokens than recorded, causing later claimers to lose out.\n\n#### Affected Token Examples\n\nThis vulnerability affects any FoT token that gets whitelisted. Real-world tokens include:\n- **PAXG**: Gold-backed token with transfer fees\n- **Deflationary tokens**: Many DeFi tokens burn on transfer\n- **Reflection tokens**: SafeMoon clones that redistribute fees\n\nIf governance whitelists any such token without awareness of this bug, users will lose funds.\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\n#### Option 1: Measure Actual Receipt (Recommended)\n\nModify `increaseTokenBalance()` to credit only what was actually received:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    \n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender)) {\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    }\n    \n    uint256 balanceAfter = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    uint256 actualReceived = balanceAfter - balanceBefore;\n    \n    // Credit only what was actually received\n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + actualReceived);\n}\n```\n\nApply the same pattern to `_pullTokens()`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _pullTokens(address creator, address rewardToken, uint256 campaignAmount, uint256 campaignAmountMinusFees) internal {\n    // ... fee handling ...\n    \n    uint256 distributorBalanceBefore = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(distributor);\n    \n    IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, distributor, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n    \n    uint256 actualSent = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(distributor) - distributorBalanceBefore;\n    \n    // Verify minimum received or adjust campaign amount\n    require(actualSent >= minAcceptable, \"Insufficient tokens received\");\n}\n```\n\n#### Option 2: Reject FoT Tokens\n\nIf supporting FoT tokens is not desired, explicitly reject them:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    \n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender)) {\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    }\n    \n    uint256 actualReceived = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;\n    \n    // Reject FoT tokens\n    require(actualReceived == amount, \"Fee-on-transfer tokens not supported\");\n    \n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + amount);\n}\n```\n\n#### Option 3: Governance Warning\n\nAt minimum, add documentation and governance procedures:\n- Clearly document that FoT tokens are not supported\n- Add validation in `setRewardTokenMinAmounts()` to verify token behavior before whitelisting\n- Emit warnings when tokens with non-standard behavior are detected",
    "proof_of_concept": "##  Proof of Concept\n\n### Overview\n\nThis PoC demonstrates how fee-on-transfer tokens break the accounting:\n1. Multiple users deposit the same FoT token\n2. Each deposit creates a small deficit (1% in this case)\n3. Early withdrawers get their full amount\n4. The last user cannot withdraw everything - they bear the accumulated deficit\n\n### Step-by-Step Scenario\n\n**Token Setup:**\n- FoT token with 1% transfer fee\n- Fee goes to a collector address (not relevant to the bug)\n\n**Deposit Phase:**\n| User | Deposits | Contract Receives | creatorBalance |\n|------|----------|------------------|----------------|\n| Alice | 1000 | 990 | 1000 |\n| Bob | 1000 | 990 | 1000 |\n| Charlie | 1000 | 990 | 1000 |\n| **Totals** | | **2970** | **3000** |\n\n**Withdrawal Phase:**\n| User | Withdraws | Contract Has | Result |\n|------|-----------|--------------|--------|\n| Alice | 1000 | 2970 → 1970 | SUCCESS |\n| Bob | 1000 | 1970 → 970 | SUCCESS |\n| Charlie | 1000 | 970 | FAIL (insufficient) |\n\n**Charlie's Loss:**\n- Charlie deposited 1000 tokens\n- Charlie can only withdraw 970 tokens\n- Charlie loses 30 tokens (the accumulated 1% fees from all deposits)\n\n### PoC Code\n\nFirst, the mock FoT token (`contracts/mock/MockFeeOnTransferToken.sol`):\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract MockFeeOnTransferToken is ERC20 {\n    uint256 public constant FEE_BPS = 100; // 1% fee\n    uint256 public constant BPS_DENOMINATOR = 10000;\n    \n    address public feeCollector;\n    \n    constructor(string memory name, string memory symbol, address _feeCollector) ERC20(name, symbol) {\n        feeCollector = _feeCollector;\n    }\n    \n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n    \n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool) {\n        uint256 fee = (amount * FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;\n        uint256 amountAfterFee = amount - fee;\n        \n        if (fee > 0) super.transfer(feeCollector, fee);\n        return super.transfer(to, amountAfterFee);\n    }\n    \n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool) {\n        uint256 fee = (amount * FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;\n        uint256 amountAfterFee = amount - fee;\n        \n        _spendAllowance(from, _msgSender(), amount);\n        if (fee > 0) _transfer(from, feeCollector, fee);\n        _transfer(from, to, amountAfterFee);\n        \n        return true;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe PoC test (`test/c4/H04_FeeOnTransfer_PoC.t.sol`):\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Test } from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport { ERC1967Proxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\nimport { DistributionCreator } from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport { MockAccessControl } from \"../../contracts/mock/MockAccessControl.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport { MockFeeOnTransferToken } from \"../../contracts/mock/MockFeeOnTransferToken.sol\";\n\ncontract H04_FeeOnTransfer_PoC is Test {\n    DistributionCreator public creator;\n    MockFeeOnTransferToken public fotToken;\n    MockAccessControl public accessControl;\n    \n    address public governor = makeAddr(\"governor\");\n    address public guardian = makeAddr(\"guardian\");\n    address public feeCollector = makeAddr(\"feeCollector\");\n    address public distributor = makeAddr(\"distributor\");\n    \n    address public alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n    address public bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");\n    address public charlie = makeAddr(\"charlie\");\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        fotToken = new MockFeeOnTransferToken(\"FeeToken\", \"FOT\", feeCollector);\n        \n        accessControl = new MockAccessControl();\n        accessControl.toggleGovernor(governor);\n        accessControl.toggleGuardian(guardian);\n        \n        DistributionCreator impl = new DistributionCreator();\n        creator = DistributionCreator(address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(impl), \"\")));\n        creator.initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControl)), distributor, 0);\n        \n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(fotToken);\n        amounts[0] = 1e18;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        fotToken.mint(alice, 1000 ether);\n        fotToken.mint(bob, 1000 ether);\n        fotToken.mint(charlie, 1000 ether);\n    }\n    \n    function test_FeeOnTransfer_Insolvency() public {\n        console.log(\"=== H-04 PoC: Fee-on-Transfer Causes Insolvency ===\");\n        console.log(\"Token: 1%% transfer fee\\n\");\n        \n        // Step 1: Alice deposits\n        console.log(\"[Step 1] Alice deposits 1,000 tokens\");\n        uint256 contractBefore = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        \n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        fotToken.approve(address(creator), 1000 ether);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(alice, address(fotToken), 1000 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        uint256 actualReceived = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator)) - contractBefore;\n        console.log(\"  Contract received: %s tokens (1%% fee taken)\", actualReceived / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  Alice's creatorBalance: %s tokens (INFLATED!)\", creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(fotToken)) / 1e18);\n        \n        // Step 2: Bob deposits\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 2] Bob deposits 1,000 tokens\");\n        contractBefore = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        \n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        fotToken.approve(address(creator), 1000 ether);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(bob, address(fotToken), 1000 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        actualReceived = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator)) - contractBefore;\n        console.log(\"  Contract received: %s tokens\", actualReceived / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  Bob's creatorBalance: %s tokens\", creator.creatorBalance(bob, address(fotToken)) / 1e18);\n        \n        // Step 3: Charlie deposits\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 3] Charlie deposits 1,000 tokens\");\n        \n        vm.startPrank(charlie);\n        fotToken.approve(address(creator), 1000 ether);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(charlie, address(fotToken), 1000 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        // Step 4: Show the accounting problem\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 4] Accounting Analysis - THE PROBLEM\");\n        \n        uint256 totalRecorded = \n            creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(fotToken)) +\n            creator.creatorBalance(bob, address(fotToken)) +\n            creator.creatorBalance(charlie, address(fotToken));\n        uint256 actualBalance = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        uint256 deficit = totalRecorded - actualBalance;\n        \n        console.log(\"  Total recorded balances: %s tokens\", totalRecorded / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  Actual contract balance: %s tokens\", actualBalance / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  DEFICIT: %s tokens\", deficit / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"\\n  The contract OWES more than it HAS!\");\n        \n        // Step 5 & 6: Early withdrawers succeed\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 5] Alice withdraws 1,000 tokens -> SUCCESS\");\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(alice, address(fotToken), alice, 1000 ether);\n        console.log(\"  Contract balance now: %s tokens\", fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator)) / 1e18);\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 6] Bob withdraws 1,000 tokens -> SUCCESS\");\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(bob, address(fotToken), bob, 1000 ether);\n        console.log(\"  Contract balance now: %s tokens\", fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator)) / 1e18);\n        \n        // Step 7: Charlie is the victim\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 7] Charlie tries to withdraw 1,000 tokens -> FAILS!\");\n        \n        uint256 charlieRecorded = creator.creatorBalance(charlie, address(fotToken));\n        uint256 contractRemaining = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        \n        console.log(\"  Charlie's creatorBalance: %s tokens\", charlieRecorded / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  Contract only has: %s tokens\", contractRemaining / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  SHORTFALL: %s tokens\", (charlieRecorded - contractRemaining) / 1e18);\n        \n        vm.startPrank(charlie);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(charlie, address(fotToken), charlie, 1000 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n  Charlie's withdrawal REVERTED!\");\n        \n        // Step 8: Charlie withdraws what's left\n        console.log(\"\\n[Step 8] Charlie withdraws whatever is left\");\n        \n        vm.prank(charlie);\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(charlie, address(fotToken), charlie, contractRemaining);\n        \n        console.log(\"  Charlie could only get: %s tokens\", contractRemaining / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"  Charlie's LOSS: %s tokens\", (charlieRecorded - contractRemaining) / 1e18);\n        \n        // Summary\n        console.log(\"\\n=== SUMMARY ===\");\n        console.log(\"Each user deposited: 1,000 tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Alice final balance: ~990 tokens (normal 1%% withdrawal fee)\");\n        console.log(\"Bob final balance: ~990 tokens (normal 1%% withdrawal fee)\");\n        console.log(\"Charlie final balance: ~960 tokens (EXTRA 30 token loss!)\");\n        console.log(\"\\nCharlie lost 30 EXTRA tokens because he withdrew last\");\n        console.log(\"from an insolvent contract.\");\n    }\n    \n    function test_Deficit_Scales_With_Users() public {\n        console.log(\"\\n=== BONUS: Deficit scales with user count ===\\n\");\n        \n        uint256 numUsers = 10;\n        address[] memory users = new address[](numUsers);\n        \n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < numUsers; i++) {\n            users[i] = makeAddr(string(abi.encodePacked(\"user\", i)));\n            fotToken.mint(users[i], 1000 ether);\n            \n            vm.startPrank(users[i]);\n            fotToken.approve(address(creator), 1000 ether);\n            creator.increaseTokenBalance(users[i], address(fotToken), 1000 ether);\n            vm.stopPrank();\n        }\n        \n        uint256 totalRecorded;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < numUsers; i++) {\n            totalRecorded += creator.creatorBalance(users[i], address(fotToken));\n        }\n        \n        uint256 actual = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        uint256 deficit = totalRecorded - actual;\n        \n        console.log(\"Users: %s\", numUsers);\n        console.log(\"Total recorded: %s tokens\", totalRecorded / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"Actual balance: %s tokens\", actual / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"Total deficit: %s tokens\", deficit / 1e18);\n        console.log(\"\\nWith more users, the last withdrawers lose more!\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Running the PoC\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-test \"test_FeeOnTransfer_Insolvency|test_Deficit_Scales_With_Users\" -vvv\n```\n\n### Expected Output\n\n```\n[PASS] test_FeeOnTransfer_Insolvency() (gas: 294199)\nLogs:\n  === H-04 PoC: Fee-on-Transfer Causes Insolvency ===\n  Token: 1% transfer fee\n\n  [Step 1] Alice deposits 1,000 tokens\n    Contract received: 990 tokens (1% fee taken)\n    Alice's creatorBalance: 1000 tokens (INFLATED!)\n\n  [Step 2] Bob deposits 1,000 tokens\n    Contract received: 990 tokens\n   